    Q2.s <span class="lini-tok-op">-</span> <span class="lini-tok-punct">|</span><span class="lini-tok-type">gnd</span><span class="lini-tok-punct">|</span>
    Q2.d <span class="lini-tok-op">-</span> J4.p3
    Q2.d <span class="lini-tok-op">-</span> D8.a <span class="lini-tok-op">-</span> <span class="lini-tok-punct">|</span><span class="lini-tok-type-user">v24</span><span class="lini-tok-punct">|</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// The fan header reads down the way its wires leave. Both upward chains</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// turn off their pins, so both take a lane, and the lane order is the</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// pins' own [SPEC 16.1]: the top screw is the deeper one along the ray, so</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// the rail keeps the inner column and the tach steps outside it — which is</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// what lets the tach's lead cross the rail's column below where it is</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// live. The switched return takes the bottom screw, and its run to the</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// drain crosses nothing.</span>
    J4.p1 <span class="lini-tok-op">-</span> <span class="lini-tok-punct">|</span><span class="lini-tok-type-user">v24</span><span class="lini-tok-punct">|</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// The tach net is named first, and the pull-up taps the name: two wires to</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// one label merge at its connection point [SPEC 16.5], so the resistor</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// stands off the tach trace instead of queueing in a second lane beside the</span>
    <span class="lini-tok-comment">// connector.</span>
